title: 8. The plan is the one record. Missions, readings and reports link to it and never copy it.
pid: 752bfac7-f40b-451e-8ef1-fe4852dc1b0f
body: |2-
  After building, its state becomes 'built', and it stays as the
  record of why. A decision changed later is edited where it stands,
  with a line saying when and why; Git keeps the old words. What the
  code records (what changed, the contracts in 'docs/') the plan
  links to and does not repeat. Each owner whose territory the plan
  changed links it from its map.
  Rests on: read (Nygard: one decision per record, kept with the
  work; Oxide: a committed RFD describes how the system now works).
  Ours: editing in place, departing from Nygard and Rust, who keep
  old records and supersede them, because here Git keeps the history
  and a second note on one thing is a loss.
